# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:In Search of the Myreque" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting Out
0	section	Vanstrom Klause
1	line	Vanstrom Klause	Hello there. The name's Vanstrom Klause. How goes it stranger?
1	line	Player	Quite well, thanks for asking. How about you?
1	line	Vanstrom Klause	Hmm, well, I am a little concerned about some friends of mine. They're in dire need of some assistance, but I'm at a loss as to how I can help them.
1	line	Player	What friends are these?
1	line	Vanstrom Klause	It's a personal tragedy that I have yet to meet them in the flesh. But their exploits make mouth watering stories... The real meat and drink of high adventure and daring... So they say.
1	line	Player	What does that mean exactly? I mean, I have some stories. I'm quite a hero myself, you may actually be talking about me?
1	line	Vanstrom Klause	They're a group of rebels fighting against the vampyres that rule over Morytania. They're known as the Myreque. Some people call them terrorists while others call them freedom fighters!
1	line	Player	I see. And you want to help them?
1	line	Vanstrom Klause	Of course. I'm a big fan of their cause. I was hoping to supply them with some new weapons. Alas, I find that I'm rather lacking in ability when it comes to this kind of thing!
1	select	Start the In Search of the Myreque quest?
1	option	Yes.
2	line	Player	Well perhaps I could take these weapons to the Myreque. What do they need?
2	line	Vanstrom Klause	Really? You would help?
2	line	Vanstrom Klause	I was hoping to deliver some steel to them. A longsword, two shortswords, a dagger, a mace and a warhammer.
2	line	Vanstrom Klause	Though if you wish to do this, I'm afraid you'll need to acquire the weapons yourself. My efforts to procure them have been rather unsuccessful.
2	line	Player	Right. Get some steel weapons and take them to the Myreque. Where can I find them?
2	line	Vanstrom Klause	The vampyres are always hunting them, so they keep themselves hidden. I hear the boatman in Mort'ton has dealings with them though.
2	line	Player	Well I'd better get going then.
2	line	Vanstrom Klause	How wonderful! Perhaps the people of Morytania now have an additional hero that they can come to rely on?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	What else do you know about the Myreque?
3	line	Player	What else do you know about the Myreque?
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	There's always some evil heel ready to grind the face of humanity into the dirt. Here in Morytania, it's the vampyres! They rule over the region with an iron fist, killing any who oppose them.
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	The Myreque are the only ones brave enough to stand up to them. They stay in the shadows though, lest the vampyres track them down!
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	No one knows for sure how many of them there are. The group hiding in Mort Myre supposedly has six members. There are whispers of more in other parts of Morytania though.
3	line	Player	And this group in Mort Myre? They're who the weapons are for?
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	Yes, indeed! The Myreque are almost certainly able to handle themselves... But they need the tools to do it!
3	action	other
2	option	Remind me, what weapons do I need?
3	line	Player	Remind me, what weapons do I need?
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	You've forgotten already? Ha! That's funny! But I do understand, my memory isn't what it was either!
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	I'd suggest a longsword, two shortswords, a dagger, a mace and a warhammer, all made of steel.
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	You'll need to obtain the weapons yourself. Fear not though! If you return to me here once you've found them, I'll be sure to give you a nice surprise in return for your help!
3	action	other
2	option	Where can I find this boatman?
3	line	Player	Where can I find this boatman?
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	I hear he lives in Mort'ton. You'll find the town south of here, through Mort Myre. It's a nasty place, but where isn't in Morytania?
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	Most of the town has supposedly fallen to some strange affliction. The boatman is apparently one of the few healthy people left!
3	line	Player	And you say he's had dealings with the Myreque?
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	So I hear. There are many who sympathise with their movement. Rumour is that this boatman's been ferrying supplies to their hideout, somewhere in Mort Myre!
3	action	other
2	option	I'd better be off.
3	line	Player	I'd better be off.
3	action	end
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	I wish I could help, but I'm busy at the moment.
2	line	Vanstrom Klause	Oh well, I'm sure someone will be along to help soon. Thanks for even considering it though.
2	action	end
