0	section	Convincing Cyreg Paddlehorn
0	section	Talking to Cyreg
1	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Hello there friend.
1	line	Player	Hello there. I'm guessing you're the boatman?
1	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Well I am 'a' boatman. I don't know about 'the' boatman though. Why do you ask anyway?
1	line	Player	I hear you have dealings with the Myreque. I was hoping to take some weapons to them.
1	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Hmm, I'm sure I don't know what you're talking about.
1	line	Player	Come on, I know you're in cahoots with them. It's important that I get these weapons to them.
1	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Well... Okay, I may have done some work for them before. It's too dangerous now though. I'm sorry, I can't help you.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Oh come on, you can tell me!
2	line	Player	Oh come on, you can tell me!
2	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	I'm sorry, I just can't... They're watching us you know... Eyes everywhere!
2	action	other
1	option	Well, I guess they'll just die without weapons.
2	line	Player	Well, I guess they'll just die without weapons.
2	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Hmm, you don't seem too concerned about their welfare. I'm glad I didn't tell you where they are. In any case, they're resourceful, they can look after themselves.
2	line	Player	What's that supposed to mean?
2	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	They're resourceful folks, that's all I'm saying. The leader of their group, Veliaf, looks after them well.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Oh come on, you can tell me!
3	action	above
3	action	previous
2	option	Resourceful enough to get their own steel weapons?
3	line	Player	Resourceful enough to get their own steel weapons?
3	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Maybe they are... What do you care anyway? They've been up against it ever since they got started.
3	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	All of 'em have suffered more loss and heartache than you'll ever know. Now, leave me be!
3	select	Select an option
3	option	What have they been up against?
4	line	Player	What have they been up against?
4	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	You're clearly not from around here or you wouldn't be asking such foolish questions.
4	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Drakan. That's what they've been up against.
4	line	Player	Drakan?
4	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Lord Lowerniel Drakan. Leader of the vampyres and ruler of Morytania. His reign over these lands means we all live in fear.
4	action	other
3	option	What kind of loss and heartache have they suffered?
4	line	Player	What kind of loss and heartache have they suffered?
4	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	The worst kind. Most have lost members of their family.
4	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Take Sani Piliu for example. she was orphaned overnight when a vampyre went on the rampage. Imagine that, losing your entire family in one night. Terrible!
4	line	Player	It sounds awful... Who is Sani Piliu?
4	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	She's the only female member of the Myreque. Her agility and light fingers have got them out of quite a few sticky situations.
4	action	other
3	option	If you don't tell me, their deaths are on your head!
4	line	Player	If you don't tell me, their deaths are on your head!
4	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	There's death aplenty in this forsaken place... What do I care that some fool hardy vigilantes decided to go it alone against the Drakans?
4	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Stupidity of youth is to blame. I won't carry it on my shoulders!
4	select	Select an option
4	option	One mans vigilante is another mans freedom fighter!
5	line	Player	One man's vigilante is another man's freedom fighter!
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Aye, you can see it from both sides I suppose. But many of us consider it fool hardy to fight for something we'll never get.
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	I remember a conversation I had with Polmafi, a scholar, such as he was. Even he agrees that the chances are slim.
5	line	Player	Polmafi? Who's he?
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Polmafi Ferdygris is one of the Myreque. He's a technical sort and advises on all sorts of things to Veliaf. He was a scholar before he became a renegade.
5	action	other
4	option	What do you know of the Drakans?
5	line	Player	What do you know of the Drakans?
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	They're the family that leads the vampyres. They're the ones to whom the blood tithes are paid. Too much I have told you already!
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Ignorance is better than these truths I tell you! I can pretend once more that I am a free man and some relief from this gloom can I feel again.
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Be gone with you now and leave me with my dreams.
5	action	other
4	option	What kind of a man are you to say that you don't care?
5	line	Player	What kind of a man are you to say that you don't care?
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Don't dare to judge me young fool... what do you know of the heartache I carry? I want to help them! I did help them! But my part is done now. To do any more is to risk death!
5	line	Player	You're risking death either way. Better to risk it and help the cause, than to stand by and do nothing.
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Hmmm. Very well, if you would take your chance to help these strangers, who am I to stop you?
5	line	Player	So you'll help me? Will you take me to them?
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	No, I won't take you, but you can use my boat.
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	You'll be going through Mort Myre though, so I won't be letting you go unless you've got some defence against the ghasts.
5	cond	If the player does not have a druid pouch in their inventory:
6	line	Player	I don't have anything which I can use against them.
6	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Well return to me once you have.
6	action	end
5	cond	If the player has a Druid Pouch in their inventory:
6	box	You show the boatman your druid pouch.
6	line	Player	I have this druid pouch! This turns the ghasts visible and I can kill them once I can see them.
6	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Very well, you can go! But you'll need to bring me six wooden planks first.
6	line	Player	What for?
6	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	The boat took some damage on my last trip. It needs repairing. There's also a bridge you'll need to cross later in your journey. It's rotten and will likely need repairs.
6	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Three of the planks are for the boat and three are for the bridge. I suggest you bring some tools and steel nails along as well.
6	select	Select an option
6	option	Here are some planks for you.
7	line	Player	Here are some planks for you.
7	box	The boatman takes three wooden planks from you and uses them to fix his boat.
7	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Right. You can take the boat. Just jump in when you're ready to leave.
7	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Go as far north as you can and you'll arrive at the Hollows. Keep heading north on foot, over the rotten bridge, and you'll eventually reach an odd looking tree. That is where you'll find the Myreque.
7	action	end
6	option	I'll be back later.
6	line	Player	I'll be back later.
4	option	Why do you say that this place is forsaken?
5	line	Player	Why do you say that this place is forsaken?
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	All of these lands are forsaken of Saradomin's kindness, only cold death from evil do we now feel.
5	line	Cyreg Paddlehorn	Those lucky ones to the west of the Salve little realise their fate if the river should one day become tainted.
5	action	other
4	option	Okay, thanks.
5	action	below
3	option	I just want to help them, I think they need help.
4	action	below
