1	line	Harold Evans	Hey! Who are you and why are you here?
1	line	Player	It's okay. I'm a friend. I'm here to deliver some weapons to you.
1	line	Harold Evans	Weapons? You'd better talk to Veliaf then. I'll be keeping an eye on you though, so don't go trying anything.
1	action	end
0	section	Speaking to Myreque members before speaking to Veliaf
0	section	Harold Evans
1	line	Harold Evans	I'm keeping my eye on you. Nothing personal. We just need to be careful with newcomers. Anyway, Veliaf will want to speak to you.
1	action	end
0	section	Radigad Ponfit
1	line	Radigad Ponfit	Greetings! Good to see some new blood. You'd better speak with Veliaf. He's in charge here.
1	action	end
0	section	Polmafi Ferdygris
1	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	Hello there. Here to help the cause are you? Speak to Veliaf. He'll sort you out.
1	action	end
0	section	Sani Piliu
1	line	Sani Piliu	Hi there. You're new here aren't you? You'd best go and talk with Veliaf.
1	action	end
0	section	Ivan Strom
1	line	Ivan Strom	Oh... Hello. Sorry, but I'm not sure if I'm supposed to be talking to you. You'd better speak to Veliaf.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Veliaf
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Veliaf Hurtz	You... I saw you come in. Harold didn't kill you though so I'm guessing you're no enemy. Who are you?
1	line	Player	I'm {player}. Don't worry, I'm a friend. I was asked to bring you some weapons.
1	line	Veliaf Hurtz	It's true that we could do with some supplies. Thank you for bringing them here. I'll have a proper look over them in a moment but there's something I must finish first.
1	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Feel free to introduce yourself to the others in the meantime.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Veliaf before speaking to all other myreque members
1	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Ah, well met. We'll discuss those weapons shortly. I need to finish something first though. Feel free to introduce yourself to the others in the meantime.
1	action	end
0	section	Speaking to Myreque members
0	section	Harold Evans
1	cond	If first time speaking:
2	line	Harold Evans	Hello there. Forgive me if I seem cautious of you. We just need to be careful with newcomers.
2	line	Player	It's fine. Do you mind if I ask a few questions?
2	action	continue
1	cond	If speaking again:
2	line	Harold Evans	Hello there. What can I do for you?
2	line	Player	I'd like to ask a few questions if that's okay?
2	action	continue
1	line	Harold Evans	Sure. I'll do my best to answer them.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	What's your job here?
2	line	Player	What's your job here?
2	line	Harold Evans	Cheating death seems to be my main role. I'm the main fighter for the group so I'm always in the thick of it. It's gone okay for me so far though.
2	action	other
1	option	What can you tell me about this group?
2	line	Player	What can you tell me about this group?
2	line	Harold Evans	We're a good team, though many of the others haven't had any proper training before. I used to be in a militia so I've been trying to share my knowledge as best I can.
2	line	Harold Evans	In most cases we end up having to improvise though. Thankfully, this lot are good at that. Ivan over there, he saved our bacon in a recent run in with some juves.
2	line	Player	Juves? What are they?
2	line	Harold Evans	Juveniles, the lowest form of vampyre. We come across them quite often around here. They may be the weakest vampyres but they're still very dangerous.
2	line	Harold Evans	They're stronger and faster than many well trained soldiers, and twice as bloodthirsty.
2	action	other
1	option	What's your grasp of the situation?
2	line	Player	What's your grasp of the situation?
2	line	Harold Evans	The situation is grave. It would be dangerous to think differently.
2	line	Harold Evans	We're really up against it, but we have no choice. This is a battle for our very existence and we need to employ any tactics to achieve our goal.
2	action	other
1	option	Have you heard any rumours?
2	line	Player	Have you heard any rumours?
2	line	Harold Evans	Yes, I hear them all the time. I don't pay any attention to them though.
2	action	other
1	option	I'll be back later.
2	line	Player	I'll be back later.
2	action	end
1	option	Okay, thanks.
2	line	Player	Okay, thanks.
2	action	end
0	section	Radigad Ponfit
1	cond	If first time speaking:
2	line	Radigad Ponfit	Ah, I see you've introduced yourself to Veliaf. Are you planning to join the fray against the Drakans?
2	line	Player	Maybe. I'd like to ask a few questions if that's okay?
2	action	continue
1	cond	If speaking again:
2	line	Radigad Ponfit	Hello again! How can I be of service to you?
2	line	Player	I'd like to ask you few questions.
2	action	continue
1	line	Radigad Ponfit	Sure, go ahead. I'll answer as best I can.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	What's your job here?
2	line	Player	What's your job here?
2	line	Radigad Ponfit	I help with anything I can. I used to be a mercenary before joining the Myreque so I know my way around a blade. I've relied on Veliaf's sword arm many a time. I like to think that he can rely on mine.
2	action	other
1	option	What can you tell me about the Myreque?
2	line	Player	What can you tell me about the Myreque?
2	line	Radigad Ponfit	We're the only resistance against the vampyres. We're seriously outnumbered though. Veliaf doesn't like to hear us saying 'hopeless' but that's our situation at the minute.
2	action	other
1	option	What're your plans for the future?
2	line	Player	What're your plans for the future?
2	line	Radigad Ponfit	That's more a question for Veliaf. Ultimately though, our goal is to rid Morytania of the vampyres so that we might reclaim our right to exist.
2	line	Radigad Ponfit	For me personally, I hope that more people will join our ranks soon. Strengh comes in numbers after all.
2	action	other
1	option	Have you heard any rumours?
2	line	Player	Have you heard any rumours?
2	line	Radigad Ponfit	I have. Something you might find interesting is that Safalaan Hallow, the leader of another Myreque group, has apparently managed to sneak one of his people into the vampyre capital, Darkmeyer.
2	line	Radigad Ponfit	I'm not sure how true that is. It would be great though!
2	action	other
1	option	I'll be back later.
2	line	Player	I'll be back later.
2	action	end
1	option	Okay, thanks.
2	line	Player	Okay, thanks.
2	action	end
0	section	Polmafi Ferdygris
1	cond	If first time speaking:
2	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	Ah, I see you've introduced yourself to Veliaf. Now, what can I do for you?
2	line	Player	Do you mind if I ask a few questions?
2	action	continue
1	cond	If speaking again:
2	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	Salutations! How are you?
2	line	Player	Fine thanks. I'd like to ask a few questions if that's okay?
2	action	continue
1	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	Not at all. I'm sure I'll be able to help.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	What are you doing here?
2	line	Player	What are you doing here?
2	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	I'm a key advisor to Veliaf. He seeks my council on many issues before we engage the enemy. Not that we do that very often. Our foes heavily outnumber us.
2	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	We don't give up though. After all, all that is required for evil to survive is for good people to do nothing.
2	action	other
1	option	What can you tell me about the Myreque?
2	line	Player	What can you tell me about the Myreque?
2	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	Well there's multiple groups of us. Even we don't know exactly how many. The less we know about our allies, the less we can reveal to the vampyres if captured.
2	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	Veliaf leads this group. We operate throughout Mort Myre and the surrounding villages. He reports to Calsidiu who is the head of our resistance.
2	action	other
1	option	What do you know about Morytania?
1	line	Player	What do you know about Morytania?
1	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	All the land on this side of the Salve is known as Morytania. Humans and vampyres are the main occupants of the region, though other races also live out here.
1	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	The humans here live like cattle with the vampyres taking regular blood tithes to keep themselves fed. All in all, it's a dire place. Though we hope to change that.
2	action	other
1	option	Have you heard any rumours?
2	line	Player	Have you heard any rumours?
2	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	Yes, I hear them all the time. They're neither correct or even all that interesting though.
2	action	other
1	option	I'll be back later.
2	line	Player	I'll be back later.
2	action	end
1	option	Okay, thanks.
2	line	Player	Okay, thanks.
2	action	end
0	section	Sani Piliu
1	cond	If first time speaking:
2	line	Sani Piliu	Hello. Very nice to meet you! The name's Sani Piliu. What's yours?
2	line	Player	I'm {player}. Nice to meet you Sani.
2	line	Sani Piliu	The pleasure's all mine! I've got a good feeling about you. I reckon you're going to do great things for us! You have a powerful aura. Sorry, that must seem really strange.
2	line	Player	Well, perhaps a little. It's nice of you to say so in any case though. I'd like to ask a few questions if that's okay?
2	action	continue
1	cond	If speaking again:
2	line	Sani Piliu	Oh, hello {player}. Nice to see you again! How's things?
2	line	Player	Fine thanks. Do you mind if I ask a few questions?
2	action	continue
1	line	Sani Piliu	Sure, go ahead. I'll answer as best I can.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Tell me a bit about yourself.
2	line	Player	Tell me a bit about yourself.
2	line	Sani Piliu	There's not much to tell really. I was nine years old when my family was ripped to pieces by a vampyre.
2	line	Sani Piliu	One moment I was a happy member of a loving family, the next I was an orphan living a hand to mouth existence.
2	line	Sani Piliu	Somehow I managed to get by, eking out a living wherever I could. People took pity on me and I earnt food by helping them out.
2	line	Sani Piliu	I quickly found I had a very useful set of skills and there were plenty of people willing to pay for them.
2	line	Sani Piliu	I bumped into Veliaf in Canifis. He saw that I would be an asset to the Myreque and invited me to join. I said yes of course. I couldn't turn down the chance to fight against those who took away my family.
2	action	other
1	option	What can you tell me about the Myreque?
2	line	Player	What can you tell me about the Myreque?
2	line	Sani Piliu	Well Veliaf is the leader of our group. We're not the only ones in Morytania though. Veliaf reports to someone called Calsidiu who's in charge of all the Myreque. I've never met any of the others though.
2	line	Sani Piliu	Our hope is to one day bring an end to the reign of Lowerniel Drakan and his vampyres.
2	line	Sani Piliu	For now though, we're just trying to find any weaknesses we can take advantage of. We need to know how to kill them before we take the war to them!
2	line	Player	You make it sound easy!
2	line	Sani Piliu	With determination you can achieve great things. However, Veliaf always tells us not to underestimate the enemy. I've made that mistake before. I won't be making it again.
2	action	other
1	option	What's going on in Morytania?
2	line	Player	What's going on in Morytania?
2	line	Sani Piliu	The entire region is ruled over by Lowerniel Drakan and his family. Everyone living here must pay blood tithes to the vampyres. The tithes keep the vampyres fed and ensure that people are too weak to oppose them.
2	line	Sani Piliu	That's where we come in. We won't just offer our family members to the Drakans as a weekly snack. We're going to fight back!
2	action	other
1	option	Is this your main camp?
2	line	Player	Is this your main camp?
2	line	Sani Piliu	It's our only camp! At least, for our group. I know there's more Myreque in other parts of Morytania but I don't know exactly where.
2	action	other
1	option	I'll be back later.
2	line	Player	I'll be back later.
2	action	end
1	option	Okay, thanks.
2	line	Player	Okay, thanks.
2	action	end
0	section	Ivan Strom
1	cond	If first time speaking:
2	line	Player	Hi there. Veliaf said that I should introduce myself to everyone.
2	line	Ivan Strom	Okay. Well my name is Ivan. It's nice to meet you.
2	line	Player	Would you mind if I asked you a few questions?
2	action	continue
1	cond	If speaking again:
2	line	Ivan Strom	Oh, hello again. How are you?
2	line	Player	Fine thanks. Would you mind if I asked you a few questions?
2	action	continue
1	line	Ivan Strom	That's fine. I don't know how much I can help though.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	What are you doing here?
2	line	Player	What are you doing here?
2	line	Ivan Strom	Me personally? I shouldn't be here really. I'm training to be a priest and I was meant to travel to Paterdomus to learn from Drezel. The trip's too dangerous at the moment though.
2	line	Player	Is it really important for you to train as a priest? I'd have thought there'd be more pressing issues.
2	line	Ivan Strom	Veliaf thinks it would be useful to have a priest to advise him. I think he also wants me further away from harm until I'm more experienced.
2	action	other
1	option	What can you tell me about the Myreque?
2	line	Player	What can you tell me about the Myreque?
2	line	Ivan Strom	We're the only ones brave enough to put up a fight against the Drakans. I'm proud to be one of them.
2	line	Ivan Strom	I do worry that I might let the others down though. I'm not as skilled as they are.
2	action	other
1	option	What do you know about Morytania?
2	line	Player	What do you know about Morytania?
2	line	Ivan Strom	It's a lost land. The evil Drakan family rule all of the region. People cling to each other in fear when the blood tithes are to be paid. It's horrible!
2	line	Ivan Strom	It won't be like this forever though. The Myreque will bring light back to this dark place.
2	action	other
1	option	Have you heard any rumours?
2	line	Player	Have you heard any rumours?
2	line	Ivan Strom	Sorry, but I haven't heard anything notable recently.
2	action	other
1	option	I'll be back later.
2	line	Player	I'll be back later.
2	action	end
1	option	Okay, thanks.
2	line	Player	Okay, thanks.
2	action	end
0	section	Speaking to Veliaf after introduced to other members
1	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Well met. I see you've introduced yourself to everyone. Shall we discuss those weapons now? Or was there something else you wanted to talk about?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Let's talk about the weapons.
2	line	Player	Let's talk about the weapons.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Let's see what you have for us.
2	cond	If the player does have the weapons:
3	box	You give the weapons to Veliaf.
3	line	Veliaf Hurtz	These weapons look great! Many thanks.
3	line	Harold Evans	What the...
3	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Vampyre!
3	line	Sani Piliu	It's Vanstrom!
3	line	Player	Wait... What?
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	Well done adventurer! You led me right to them. The little dears are going to wonder which side you're on!
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	The Drakans have been wanting you lot dealt with for a while now. We wouldn't want to disappoint them, would we?
3	line	Sani Piliu	We're dead!
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	Quite right.
3	line	Harold Evans	No!
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	Sorry Harold, you too!
3	line	Vanstrom Klause	And now... A little gift for the rest of you.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player does not have the weapons:
3	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Ah. I'm afraid you don't have suitable weapons for us. Sorry friend.
3	select	Select an option
3	option	What weapons do you need?
4	line	Player	What weapons do you need?
4	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Well we all have our own specialisms. We could do with a longsword, two shortswords, a dagger, a mace and a warhammer, all made from steel.
4	line	Player	Okay. I'll come back once I have them.
4	action	end
3	option	I'll be back later.
4	line	Player	I'll be back later.
4	action	end
1	option	So you're the leader of this group?
2	line	Player	So you're the leader of this group?
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	That's right. I can't say I particularly asked for it. The others look up to me though, so they decided I was the best man for the job.
2	action	other
1	option	Can you tell me about your organisation?
2	line	Player	Can you tell me about your organisation?
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Well I wouldn't say we're an organisation. We're really not that organised.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Anyway though, we're a group of Myreque freedom fighters. We're dedicated to mounting a resistance against the Drakan family and their vampyre kin.
2	action	other
1	option	What can you tell me about Morytania?
2	line	Player	What can you tell me about Morytania?
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	If legend is to be believed, it was once a beautiful place. But then Lowerniel Drakan and his vampyres arrived.
2	line	Player	Who is Lowerniel Drakan?
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Lowerniel Vergidiyad Drakan is his full name. He's the vampyre that heads up the Drakan family. Helped by his brother Ranis and his sister Vanescula, he rules over all of Morytania.
2	line	Player	You sound very bitter.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	So would you if you lost everyone dear to you at the hands of such monsters.
2	action	other
1	option	What are your plans for the future?
2	line	Player	What are your plans for the future?
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	At the moment we're maintaining a low profile here at our hideout. We were recently spotted while out on a scouting mission so we're playing it safe and lying low.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Looking further ahead, we need to build more support if we have any hope of taking on the vampyres. We also need to learn more about their weaknesses, so we can take advantage of them.
2	action	other
1	option	I'll be back later.
2	line	Player	I'll be back later.
2	action	end
1	option	Okay, thanks.
2	line	Player	Okay, thanks.
2	action	end
0	section	After defeating the skeleton hellhound
0	section	Veliaf Hurtz
1	cond	If first time speaking:
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Sani... Harold... That murderer killed them!
2	line	Player	I'm so sorry. This is all my fault.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	I don't understand though. He said you led him here. How?
2	line	Player	He was the one that asked me to bring the weapons to you. He looked like a human though.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	I'm sorry friend, but he clearly took advantage of you. Vampyres can shapeshift to look like humans. Someone from around here might have realised. You were not to know though.
2	line	Player	No. I'm still responsible though.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	The burden of what happened here is for your conscience to bear. That said, you managed to kill that pet of his. We might all be dead if not for you.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	I imagine you now see why we fight for our freedom.
2	line	Player	Yes. I think I understand. Is there anything I can do to help now? I first met Vanstrom in Canifis. I could go back and see if he's still there?
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	I suspect he will have moved on now. You're welcome to try though. I know a shortcut that you might find useful.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	If you head back into the main cave and go north you'll reach a wall. There's a hidden door in that wall that leads right into the basement of the Hair of the Dog Tavern.
2	line	Player	That's very useful. Thanks.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Once you are done, I'd appreciate you coming back here to discuss a few things. You held your own against that creature. We could use someone like you.
2	action	continue
1	cond	If speaking again:
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Need something?
2	action	continue
1	select	Select an option
1	option	I want to join your organisation.
2	line	Player	I want to join your organisation.
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	Well we could definitely use someone like you. You should go and see if Vanstrom is still in Canifis though. Come back once you're done, and we'll talk.
2	action	other
1	option	What do you plan to do now?
2	line	Player	What do you plan to do now?
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	We won't be able to stay here now that Vanstrom knows where we've been hiding. We have some time though. He'll expect that we're all dead. We'll use that time to form a plan of action.
2	action	other
1	option	How do I get out of here again?
2	line	Player	How do I get out of here again?
2	line	Veliaf Hurtz	If you head back into the main cave and go north you'll reach a wall. There's a hidden door in that wall that leads right into the basement of the Hair of the Dog Tavern.
2	action	other
1	option	Okay, thanks.
2	line	Player	Okay, thanks.
2	action	end
0	section	Radigad Ponfit
1	line	Radigad Ponfit	That monster! He killed them! We'll make them all pay!
1	action	end
0	section	Polmafi Ferdygris
1	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	This is a dark day for the Myreque.
1	line	Player	I'm so sorry for your loss.
1	line	Polmafi Ferdygris	Don't worry. No one blames you. You were tricked and that's that. It serves no useful purpose to blame any of ourselves for this.
1	action	end
0	section	Ivan Strom
1	line	Ivan Strom	Thank Saradomin you managed to kill that awful beast! I just wish we could have done more.
1	line	Player	I'm so sorry for your loss. If there's anything I can do, please let me know.
1	line	Ivan Strom	I will. Thank you.
1	action	end
0	section	Finishing Up
1	line	Stranger	Hello friend. What can I do for you?
1	line	Player	Oh, sorry. I thought you were someone else.
1	line	Stranger	Who did you think I was?
1	line	Player	I thought you were that dirty murderer Vanstrom.
1	line	Stranger	Woah! It sounds like you've got a score to settle!
1	line	Player	I definitely have!
1	action	end
